[stderr] +playwright_spec:
[stderr] +---
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Objective
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after D0002. Expand at most one
[stderr] +eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter into no more than 250 `IMP-*`
[stderr] +records, validate it, then allocate ready unassigned contracts into at most ten
[stderr] +new B-series authoring tasks with no more than seven R-series outputs each.
[stderr] +Create exactly one successor dispatcher when queued work or ready contracts
[stderr] +remain; otherwise create exactly one final audit B-series task. Exit after that
[stderr] +bounded set.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Context packet
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,
[stderr] +`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,
[stderr] +`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and
[stderr] +`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Review D0002's `dispatch_history` checkpoint and
[stderr] +only the canonical specification sections needed for a selected chapter.
[stderr] +`SHARD-02` is not eligible until `DEC-0004`/`GATE-0004` is explicitly resolved;
[stderr] +`SHARD-03` and `SHARD-04` retain their listed predecessor/gate blocks; and
[stderr] +`SHARD-05` remains held unless explicit authorisation is recorded.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Output list
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- No R-series output is preassigned. Allocate R IDs only for ready, unassigned
[stderr] +  catalogue contracts discovered after the bounded chapter check.
[stderr] +- At most ten new B-series authoring runbooks, each owning no more than seven
[stderr] +  newly assigned R-series outputs.
[stderr] +- Exactly one successor dispatcher or one final audit B-series task, selected
[stderr] +  only after the queue and ready-contract check.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Required behaviour
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Preserve all accepted work and use monotonic B/R/IMP IDs. Do not infer approval
[stderr] +from a gate or from a queued state. A selected expansion must include stable
[stderr] +requirement links, ownership, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,
[stderr] +verification, asset assessment, and canonical sources; validate coverage,
[stderr] +unique IDs, ownership, provenance, and acyclic dependencies before allocation.
[stderr] +Every new B task must provide its context packet, output list, validation,
[stderr] +checkpoint/update procedure, collision protection, and stop condition. Do not
[stderr] +create R-series files in this dispatcher.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Validation procedure
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Validate JSON, the selected chapter's 250-contract limit, unique IMP/B/R IDs,
[stderr] +dependency closure and acyclicity, ownership/path collisions, allocation
[stderr] +uniqueness, provenance, and asset metadata. Confirm each B owns at most seven R
[stderr] +IDs and that no more than ten B tasks were created. Confirm the successor/final
[stderr] +audit choice against the remaining queued chapters and ready unassigned
[stderr] +contracts. Stop and report any source conflict, missing coverage, cycle,
[stderr] +collision, unresolved authority, or need to overwrite accepted work.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Checkpoint and update procedure
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Atomically update the JSON and Markdown ledgers with chapter state, allocations,
[stderr] +counters, and the D0003 checkpoint only after validation. Retain reserved IDs
[stderr] +on repair; never renumber, replace, or rewrite an accepted B/R contract.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Collision protection
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Before creating any B, R, IMP, successor, or audit path, verify that its ID and
[stderr] +path are absent from the authoritative manifest and filesystem. On collision,
[stderr] +stop without overwriting or reusing the ID.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Stop condition
[stderr] +
[stderr] +Stop immediately after at most one chapter expansion, one allocation wave, and
[stderr] +exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a recursive
[stderr] +prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.
[stderr] +
[stderr] +## Acceptance criteria
[stderr] +
[stderr] +- The iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.
[stderr] +- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.
[stderr] +- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.
[stderr] +- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.
[stderr] +- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.
