t-privacy-and-security\"],\"catalogue_records\":[\"IMP-0012\"]},\"checkpoint\":\"cross-check all foundation ownership, dependencies, and gates before accepting the wave\",\"recovery\":\"retain R0012 and correct only its documentation contract\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"documentation concludes the foundation slice without claiming implementation or approval\",\"gated save work remains visible\"]}\n  ],\n  \"r_contracts\": [\n    {\"id\":\"R0001\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0001\",\"title\":\"Bootstrap reproducible shared project baseline\",\"dependencies\":[],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0001.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#release-definition\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0001\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0001\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No product asset work; establish only project/tooling boundaries and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"documented deterministic baseline command\",\"isolated ownership directories\",\"GATE-0001 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and path; repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0002\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0002\",\"title\":\"Enforce shared-core and adapter dependency seams\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0002.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#dependency-direction-and-state-rules\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0002\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; this is an interface and dependency-policy contract.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"forbidden core imports rejected\",\"adapter command-only fixture\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0003\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0003\",\"title\":\"Create deterministic test and fixture harness\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0003.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#observability-quality-evidence-and-release-verification\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0003\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; fixtures use non-product deterministic data.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"repeatable fixture result\",\"isolated fixture storage\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0004\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0004\",\"title\":\"Define deterministic campaign state and command contract\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0004.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#data-contract\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#commands-validation-idempotency-and-concurrency\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0004\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0003\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; state envelopes deliberately exclude authored content.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"stale and invalid commands do not mutate state\",\"duplicate interaction is idempotent\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0005\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0005\",\"title\":\"Define versioned content schema and validation boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0003\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0005.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#versioned-content-and-save-schemas\",\"specification/02-feature-model.md#domain-vocabulary-and-state-ownership\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0005\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0004\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No art/audio assets; reserve only schema/provenance fields for later original assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"valid minimal package passes\",\"invalid references fail\",\"reachability fixture\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0006\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0006\",\"title\":\"Specify local save and recovery protocol\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0006.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0006\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0004\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; protocol is data/recovery only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"fault fixtures cover write and validation failures\",\"save/cache separation\",\"GATE-0003 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID; wait for storage decision before accepting gated work\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0007\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0007\",\"title\":\"Define pure save migration runner\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\",\"R0006\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0007.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0007\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; migration fixtures retain original bytes only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"predecessors migrate once\",\"failed candidate remains intact\",\"GATE-0003 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and resume after R0006/gate closure\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0008\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0008\",\"title\":\"Bound P0 identity, authorization, and connected-service exclusions\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0008.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0008\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0003\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; a negative scope boundary.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"no identity/token/network fields\",\"future connected work remains gated\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0009\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0009\",\"title\":\"Define privacy-safe local diagnostics boundary\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0003\",\"R0006\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0009.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#empty-error-recovery-destructive-and-privacy-sensitive-states\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0009\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; local redacted records only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"consent and deletion controls\",\"payload redaction\",\"no network transport\",\"GATE-0005 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and wait for privacy gate where required\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0010\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0010\",\"title\":\"Establish semantic accessibility design tokens\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0001\",\"R0002\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0010.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#layout-visual-tokens-and-responsive-behaviour\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#accessibility-policy\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0010\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0002\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No final artwork, fonts, or icons; semantic tokens only and prohibit incidental assets.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"non-colour cues\",\"reduced motion values\",\"GATE-0002,GATE-0004 retained\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and await numeric design decisions\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0011\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0011\",\"title\":\"Create original-content provenance control\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0005\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0011.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/01-product-brief.md#originality-boundary\",\"specification/04-experience-contract.md#experience-premise-and-originality-boundary\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0011\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0005\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets are created; this contract defines provenance controls for later asset-required work.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"missing provenance rejected\",\"human creative review recorded\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this contract\"},\n    {\"id\":\"R0012\",\"catalogue_id\":\"IMP-0012\",\"title\":\"Document foundation architecture and recovery boundaries\",\"dependencies\":[\"R0002\",\"R0004\",\"R0006\",\"R0008\"],\"output_path\":\"projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/runbooks/R0012.md\",\"source_specifications\":[\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#architecture-and-requirement-traceability\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#persistence-migration-and-failure-semantics\",\"specification/03-technical-contract.md#trust-privacy-and-security\"],\"source_catalogue_ids\":[\"IMP-0012\"],\"authoring_batch\":\"B0006\",\"factory_stages\":[\"F011\",\"F012\",\"F013\"],\"asset_impact\":\"not_applicable\",\"asset_ids\":[],\"asset_brief\":\"No assets; developer-documentation closure only.\",\"acceptance_checks\":[\"all foundation ownership/dependencies/gates cross-checked\",\"does not claim release readiness\"],\"checkpoint_cadence\":\"after metadata, after draft, before manifest acceptance\",\"recovery\":\"retain ID and repair only this documentation contract\"}\n  ]\n}\n# mock-fantasy-quest-4 runbook factory handoff\n\nThis workspace is a **planning and runbook-authoring factory** for an eventual\nimplementation project. It does not contain a game implementation, product\ntest evidence, deployment, publishing, or release approval. The factory turns\nthe approved brief into bounded, reviewable implementation contracts; a later\nimplementation project chooses its stack and carries out those contracts only\nafter their gates are approved.\n\n## Read the sources in this order\n\n1. [`INITIAL.md`](INITIAL.md) is the original source of truth. It records the\n   scope, selected targets, constraints, non-goals, and unanswered questions.\n   [`PROJECT_BRIEF.md`](PROJECT_BRIEF.md) is its durable project-local copy.\n2. The canonical [specification index](specification/README.md) is the stable\n   requirement and decision system. Start with the [domain-discovery map]\n   (specification/00-domain-discovery.md): it explains why exploration, town,\n   dungeon, combat, inventory, quests, save/recovery, accessibility, web, and\n   PWA systems appear in the downstream runbooks. The canonical specification\n   must not override the original brief.\n3. The planning catalogue\u2014[`implementation-catalogue-index.md`](planning/implementation-catalogue-index.md)\n   and its authoritative [JSON](planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json)\u2014\n   maps canonical requirements to bounded `IMP-*` contracts. The audited\n   [delivery map](planning/05-delivery-map.md) and\n   [contract audit](planning/09-contract-audit.md) provide dependency and\n   closure evidence.\n\nResponsive public web and installable PWA delivery are included by default for\nthis project. All actual platform requirements, including input, storage,\noffline/update, browser support, and performance constraints, come from the\nselected targets in the original brief and the canonical platform appendix;\nthey are not inferred from \"web/PWA\" alone.\n\n## The three levels of work\n\n| Level | Purpose | Inputs and outputs | Not permission to |\n| --- | --- | --- | --- |\n| Source brief and canonical specification | Preserve P0 scope, requirements, decisions, risks, target adaptations, and traceability | `INITIAL.md`, `PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `specification/`, and `planning/` | Select gated technology, resolve an open decision, or build/release the game |\n| B-series authoring runbooks | Write bounded `R####` implementation contracts from allocated `IMP-*` records | `authoring-runbooks/`, `planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, and its Markdown ledger | Implement product code, create final assets, or claim product evidence |\n| R-series implementation runbooks | Give the eventual implementation project one small, independently verifiable contract at a time | Repository-root `runbooks/R####.md` and the evidence paths named by each contract | Bypass its dependencies or human/external gates, publish, deploy, or release |\n\nThe `Final Fantasy V` reference is a high-level party-based, turn-based\nadventure scope reference only. Never copy or request its branding, names,\nstory/lore, dialogue, maps, art, music, layouts, combat screens, or distinctive\ninteraction choreography. All creative work must be independently original and\nfollow the warm hand-painted, readable-silhouette, restrained-palette direction\nwith provenance and human creative review.\n\n## Run the factory and authoring collections\n\nRun these from the repository root. `--project mock-fantasy-quest-4` loads this\nworkspace's versioned, non-secret Supervisor configuration and uses its durable\nstate. An accepted task is skipped on a later collection run unless explicitly\nretried.\n\n### 1. Factory collection\n\nRun the F-series factory collection and discover its registered child\ncollections:\n\n```zsh\n./supervisor/.venv/bin/supervisor-run --project mock-fantasy-quest-4 --run-all --runbooks-dir runbooks\n```\n\nThe factory source collection is repository-root `runbooks/`; its child\nregistration is `runbooks/.supervisor-children/mock-fantasy-quest-4.json`.\nThe project factory state and raw, per-stage logs are under\n`.state/factory.sqlite3` and `.state/live/` respectively.\n\n### 2. B-series implementation-contract authoring\n\nRun the current B-series collection after its prerequisites are accepted:\n\n```zsh\n./supervisor/.venv/bin/supervisor-run --project mock-fantasy-quest-4 --run-all --runbooks-dir projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks\n```\n\nTo run just a dependency-ready writer, use its immutable file\u2014for example:\n\n```zsh\n./supervisor/.venv/bin/supervisor-run --project mock-fantasy-quest-4 --runbook projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\n```\n\nThe authoring collection starts at `authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md`; the\ndispatcher is `authoring-runbooks/D0001.md`. The B-series collection has its\nown `.state/authoring-runbooks.sqlite3` and `.state/live/` evidence locations.\nIts authoritative allocation ledger is\n[`planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json),\nwith [`planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md`](planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md)\nas the readable companion. Each B writer may create only its manifest-owned\nR-series paths.\n\nValidate the generated collection after each bounded wave:\n\n```zsh\npython3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py --wave B0001\npython3 projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/validate_runbook_generation.py\n```\n\nThe validator is structural authoring evidence only. Its report is terminal\noutput; retain the relevant Supervisor task result, live log, and manifest\ncheckpoint in `.state/` and `planning/`. It does not prove implementation,\nbrowser behaviour, accessibility, visual quality, or release readiness.\n\n### 3. R-series implementation contracts\n\nAfter the responsible B writer has generated an R contract, dispatch it to the\neventual implementation project through the chosen **Codex-only Supervisor\npipeline** (`SUPERVISOR_AGENT_ORDER=codex`, followed by Supervisor's configured\nindependent precheck/test/browser/visual-review/completion gates). For one\nselected contract:\n\n```zsh\n./supervisor/.venv/bin/supervisor-run --project mock-fantasy-quest-4 --runbook runbooks/R0001.md\n```\n\nFor all currently generated R-series contracts, run each manifest-owned file\nin its declared dependency order (only after every file exists):\n\n```zsh\nfind: -printf: unknown primary or operator\n\ncodex\n{\"status\":\"pass\",\"summary\":\"The gate review found no eligible queued chapter and no ready unassigned contracts: SHARD-02 remains blocked by GATE-0004, later shards retain their gates, and all existing IMP records are allocated. I\u2019m recording that bounded no-allocation iteration and creating the single required successor dispatcher.\",\"changed_files\":[],\"test_result\":\"\",\"evidence\":{\"agent_log\":\"\",\"adapter_log\":\"\",\"test_log\":\"\",\"browser_log\":\"\",\"screenshots\":[]},\"acceptance_results\":[],\"documentation\":{\"reviewed_files\":[],\"updated_files\":[],\"summary\":\"\"},\"known_limitations\":[],\"browser_coverage\":\"\",\"recommended_next_step\":\"complete\"}\napply patch\npatch: completed\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0003.md\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\n/Users/simon/Dev/github/jakowicz/runbook-generator/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.md\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md\nindex e4980b5b0d8712db21e8b286ae007aa785ea5cc7..bff8323ec64b52d3944c2ad54a5698d498097658\n--- a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/README.md\n@@ -81,8 +81,8 @@\n ./supervisor/.venv/bin/supervisor-run --project mock-fantasy-quest-4 --runbook projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/B0001.md\n ```\n \n-The authoring collection starts at `authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md`; the\n-dispatcher is `authoring-runbooks/D0001.md`. The B-series collection has its\n+The authoring collection starts at `authoring-runbooks/INITIAL.md`; the current\n+dispatcher is `authoring-runbooks/D0003.md`. The B-series collection has its\n own `.state/authoring-runbooks.sqlite3` and `.state/live/` evidence locations.\n Its authoritative allocation ledger is\n [`planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`](planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json),\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0003.md b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0003.md\nnew file mode 100644\nindex 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000..064c70a752362b4b9f67f1c95217618ceaa2fd31\n--- /dev/null\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/authoring-runbooks/D0003.md\n@@ -0,0 +1,84 @@\n+---\n+task_id: D0003\n+sequence: 10\n+title: Resume bounded implementation-runbook authoring dispatch after D0002\n+browser_impact: not_applicable\n+playwright_spec:\n+---\n+\n+## Objective\n+\n+Run one durable authoring-dispatch iteration after D0002. Expand at most one\n+eligible queued specification/catalogue chapter into no more than 250 `IMP-*`\n+records, validate it, then allocate ready unassigned contracts into at most ten\n+new B-series authoring tasks with no more than seven R-series outputs each.\n+Create exactly one successor dispatcher when queued work or ready contracts\n+remain; otherwise create exactly one final audit B-series task. Exit after that\n+bounded set.\n+\n+## Context packet\n+\n+Read `INITIAL.md`, `../PROJECT_BRIEF.md`, `../specification/README.md`,\n+`../planning/implementation-catalogue-index.json`,\n+`../planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json`, its Markdown ledger, and\n+`../../../runbooks/F014.md`. Review D0002's `dispatch_history` checkpoint and\n+only the canonical specification sections needed for a selected chapter.\n+`SHARD-02` is not eligible until `DEC-0004`/`GATE-0004` is explicitly resolved;\n+`SHARD-03` and `SHARD-04` retain their listed predecessor/gate blocks; and\n+`SHARD-05` remains held unless explicit authorisation is recorded.\n+\n+## Output list\n+\n+- No R-series output is preassigned. Allocate R IDs only for ready, unassigned\n+  catalogue contracts discovered after the bounded chapter check.\n+- At most ten new B-series authoring runbooks, each owning no more than seven\n+  newly assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Exactly one successor dispatcher or one final audit B-series task, selected\n+  only after the queue and ready-contract check.\n+\n+## Required behaviour\n+\n+Preserve all accepted work and use monotonic B/R/IMP IDs. Do not infer approval\n+from a gate or from a queued state. A selected expansion must include stable\n+requirement links, ownership, dependencies, non-goals, platform distinctions,\n+verification, asset assessment, and canonical sources; validate coverage,\n+unique IDs, ownership, provenance, and acyclic dependencies before allocation.\n+Every new B task must provide its context packet, output list, validation,\n+checkpoint/update procedure, collision protection, and stop condition. Do not\n+create R-series files in this dispatcher.\n+\n+## Validation procedure\n+\n+Validate JSON, the selected chapter's 250-contract limit, unique IMP/B/R IDs,\n+dependency closure and acyclicity, ownership/path collisions, allocation\n+uniqueness, provenance, and asset metadata. Confirm each B owns at most seven R\n+IDs and that no more than ten B tasks were created. Confirm the successor/final\n+audit choice against the remaining queued chapters and ready unassigned\n+contracts. Stop and report any source conflict, missing coverage, cycle,\n+collision, unresolved authority, or need to overwrite accepted work.\n+\n+## Checkpoint and update procedure\n+\n+Atomically update the JSON and Markdown ledgers with chapter state, allocations,\n+counters, and the D0003 checkpoint only after validation. Retain reserved IDs\n+on repair; never renumber, replace, or rewrite an accepted B/R contract.\n+\n+## Collision protection\n+\n+Before creating any B, R, IMP, successor, or audit path, verify that its ID and\n+path are absent from the authoritative manifest and filesystem. On collision,\n+stop without overwriting or reusing the ID.\n+\n+## Stop condition\n+\n+Stop immediately after at most one chapter expansion, one allocation wave, and\n+exactly one successor dispatcher or final audit task. This is not a recursive\n+prompt and must not materialise a whole-game plan.\n+\n+## Acceptance criteria\n+\n+- The iteration expands at most one eligible chapter and adds no more than 250 IMP contracts.\n+- It creates at most ten bounded B-series authoring tasks, each with at most seven assigned R-series outputs.\n+- Every created B task has its context packet, output list, validation, checkpoint/update, collision protection, and stop condition.\n+- If queued or ready work remains, exactly one successor dispatcher is created; otherwise exactly one final audit B-series task is created.\n+- IDs, manifest ownership, provenance, asset assessments, and dependencies are validated without overwriting accepted work.\ndiff --git a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\nindex 8658e5ee05d7f524f0320681a1d98c40f8af61fb..a4a3e3fe2792cfcc3d5717c695b2f05e0d4bafb5\n--- a/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\n+++ b/projects/mock-fantasy-quest-4/planning/runbook-authoring-manifest.json\n@@ -8,7 +8,8 @@\n   \"id_counters\": {\"next_authoring_batch_id\": \"B0007\", \"next_implementation_runbook_id\": \"R0013\", \"rule\": \"Never reuse, renumber, or replace an accepted B or R ID. Append new allocations using these counters only.\"},\n   \"wave\": {\"number\": 1, \"state\": \"planned\", \"checkpoint_after_each_batch\": true, \"resume_from\": \"first batch whose state is not accepted; validate accepted IDs, paths, and provenance before dispatch\", \"recovery\": \"If a batch fails, retain its IDs, mark it blocked or repairable, repair only its listed output paths, validate its contracts, then resume that same batch. Do not reallocate its R IDs.\"},\n   \"dispatch_history\": [\n-    {\"dispatcher\":\"D0001\",\"sequence\":8,\"state\":\"complete\",\"expanded_chapter\":null,\"new_imp_contract_ids\":[],\"new_authoring_batches\":[],\"ready_unassig